<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:44Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Death of Nahel: French police officer who shot dead a teenage boy to stand trial for murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d58ef71c75f9b9d9a1292e7c00de76e4ce8fd8cad1f0c2832be4727d6c2eb937</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:54:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261124-death-of-nahel-french-police-officer-who-shot-dead-a-teenage-boy-to-stand-trial-for-murder--82f340150afa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261124-death-of-nahel-french-police-officer-who-shot-dead-a-teenage-boy-to-stand-trial-for-murder" /><summary type="html">A French police officer who shot and killed 17-year-old Nahel Merzouk during a traffic stop in June 2023 will stand trial for murder following a ruling by the Versailles appeals court. Merzouk's death at the hands of the police sparked intense riots in the sprawling suburbs surrounding Paris.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>China to launch first space mission with a foreign astronaut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7069469e4ef5573d432b07f590912bb2380ca283c816064b7a4db6d197a98682</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:50:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261124-china-to-launch-first-space-mission-with-a-foreign-astronaut--c239a636435e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261124-china-to-launch-first-space-mission-with-a-foreign-astronaut" /><summary type="html">Pakistan's Muhammad Zeeshan Ali will become the first foreign astronaut to board China's Tiangong space station when the latest crew blasts off Wednesday. Ali said he would be carrying "the hopes of 250 million Pakistanis" with him.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>ICG: "It's hard to imagine" Tripoli would risk its ties with Russia by approving a Ukrainian attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d5396557e6979809102d528e54c69d1b865a8c0d6f6b3a9ac416ede8200c3b8</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T07:45:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261124-icg-it-s-hard-to-imagine-tripoli-would-risk-its-ties-with-russia-by-approving-a-ukrainian-a--57eb1b9bbd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261124-icg-it-s-hard-to-imagine-tripoli-would-risk-its-ties-with-russia-by-approving-a-ukrainian-attack" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Claudia Gazzini, International Crisis Group's Senior Analyst for Libya. The Ukrainian attack on a Russian warship off the coast of eastern Libya has raised questions about Russian and Ukrainian military activity in the country. Gazzini discusses Russia's established military presence in eastern Libya and allegations that Ukrainian forces are operating in the west. She notes that while Russia is militarily present in eastern Libya, it also maintains "good commercial ties and political ties with western authorities as well." For Gazzini, the suggestion that Tripoli would approve such an operation "just sounds a bit too hazardous."</summary></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang’s return has calmed markets but fears of an AI bubble still run deep</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c2d2e0aba4193182cb03c69b4cfd09ef4db4ef632f99cbbec4081178e7096cc</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T07:15:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-jensen-huang-s-return-has-calmed-markets-but-fears-of-an-ai-bubble-still-run-deep--4522ba2897b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-jensen-huang-s-return-has-calmed-markets-but-fears-of-an-ai-bubble-still-run-deep" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's decision to bring back Jensen Huang as CEO pushed the AI computing company's stocks up more than 30 percent Monday. But the model of circular financing increasingly underwriting the AI boom still has some analysts worried that the party can't last forever.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Collapse of COP31: 'This deal was a bad deal and better no deal than a bad deal'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ca448c38969cea7e7862eef31cae1c06f0de7b5d6fe1836f191022631df7cde</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T06:51:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261124-collapse-of-cop31-this-deal-was-a-bad-deal-and-better-no-deal-than-a-bad-deal--6e15b18a80e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261124-collapse-of-cop31-this-deal-was-a-bad-deal-and-better-no-deal-than-a-bad-deal" /><summary type="html">François Picard is joined by Ireland's former Environment Minister Eamon Ryan following the collapse of COP31 in Antalya, Turkey. “Political science trumps climate science still,” Ryan said the talks failed after the European Union and up to 100 countries refused to accept a final text that abandoned earlier commitments to transition away from fossil fuels.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>AFCON 2025: CAS set to hand down ruling on controversial final</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20cb4cf2b5a9a732b547e801165ac9a4d0011d14610697c8b4a9d56bfe473f17</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T06:35:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261124-2025-afcon-cas-set-to-hand-down-ruling-on-controversial-final--281d9c6d364c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261124-2025-afcon-cas-set-to-hand-down-ruling-on-controversial-final" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport will deliver its ruling this Tuesday on the 2025 Africa Cup of Nations final. Senegal won the match on the pitch, but Morocco were awarded the trophy following an appeal to the CAF.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Russian strikes on Ukraine’s Zaporizhzhia kill two people and wound dozens more</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec481cb362369b692dd57ad01f5e767eeca0024d0c73387405a8c411feeb721e</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T05:50:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-live-tripoli-demands-explanation-from-kyiv-for-striking-russian-ships-in-libyan-waters--e55baa58ddf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-live-tripoli-demands-explanation-from-kyiv-for-striking-russian-ships-in-libyan-waters" /><summary type="html">A Russian attack killed two people in the Ukrainian city of Zaporizhzhia overnight, regional governor Mykhailo Semikin said on Tuesday. Some 40 people, four of them children, were also wounded in the strikes, the governor added. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang's surprise return to Nvidia sparks mixed reactions in Washington</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a8b88d3ad26e8d1538ab0f47c00cea41e6031ed3f2a082c869a8f4e5f545763</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T03:16:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261124-jensen-huang-s-surprise-return-to-nvidia-sparks-mixed-reactions-in-washington--cf97921169e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261124-jensen-huang-s-surprise-return-to-nvidia-sparks-mixed-reactions-in-washington" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump praised Nvidia's decision Monday to reinstate Jensen Huang as chief executive, as Democratic leaders vowed investigations and prominent Republicans questioned whether his return posed a national security risk.</summary></entry><entry><title>US flew surveillance drone over Mexico to help capture top drug lord</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9a730858cb6e628113093c020b470b8a08d2944a06aabbfb4372fe895bcf78d</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T02:09:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-us-flew-surveillance-drone-over-mexico-to-help-capture-top-drug-lord--342d551a758c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-us-flew-surveillance-drone-over-mexico-to-help-capture-top-drug-lord" /><summary type="html">Mexican officials say the United States flew a surveillance drone over Mexican territory to help locate and capture one of the country's most wanted drug traffickers. The operation led to the arrest of Fausto Isidro Meza Flores, known as 'El Chapo Isidro'.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky urges four-way peace talks with Russia, Europe and US 'as soon as possible'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:907bfefe652935d004fb0864bce1dd9b56c7f37678599ee8d931394bc7c7c19d</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T00:30:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-zelensky-urges-four-way-peace-talks-with-russia-europe-and-us-as-soon-as-possible--354e3c5e6ad8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-zelensky-urges-four-way-peace-talks-with-russia-europe-and-us-as-soon-as-possible" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky is calling for a new round of negotiations involving Ukraine, Russia, the United States and European leaders, saying Kyiv is ready to meet as early as Tuesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>14 countries acknowledge ICJ ruling of genocide against Rohingya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:699c926f9ae8ca459c5c4779d691761c0fb698d5b610b4192b2ff2bfe9b8c77e</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T23:10:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261123-14-countries-acknowledge-icj-ruling-of-genocide-against-rohingya--1e8743cb4fa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261123-14-countries-acknowledge-icj-ruling-of-genocide-against-rohingya" /><summary type="html">Fourteen countries from Europe, Africa and Oceania have acknowledged a landmark ruling by the International Court of Justice (ICJ) that Myanmar committed genocide against its Rohingya minority, calling on the country to comply with its obligations under international law. The United Kingdom separately announced sanctions against five senior Myanmar military figures and said it would formally recognise the genocide.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>NATO vows space defence after Russia nuclear satellite report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fec33f207e3f0ddbb489119a7825c22165c4e6c40c87fd58902cddccc35a814</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T22:33:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nato-vows-space-defence-after-russia-nuclear-satellite-report--b818d8d38eb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nato-vows-space-defence-after-russia-nuclear-satellite-report" /><summary type="html">NATO chief Mark Rutte said Monday the alliance would defend against threats in space when asked about German media reports that Russia may be preparing to launch a nuclear-armed satellite. The media reports, citing unnamed German military and BND spy agency sources, said Moscow was thought to be planning such a launch in the coming weeks, giving it the capability to destroy other satellites. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Africa disappointed with COP31 outcome</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1633c3cf061102ebebc63628d32fcf8a720a9cc850da21192a27056e015b86a</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T22:14:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa-disappointed-with-cop31-outcome" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, the COP31 climate summit in Turkey has failed to reach an agreement, exposing deep divisions over fossil fuels and climate finance. Also, DR Congo's Félix Tshisekedi and Kenya's William Ruto agree to restore  relations and boost regional cooperation. And determined to help their children, parents in a South African township have transformed a discarded shipping container into a sensory room.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang reinstated as Nvidia CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2aae5b6d62d5f37685f317e6cdaff3aa9aa5c472b097dd76cc648c8ff94fcf76</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T22:10:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261123-jensen-huang-reinstated-as-nvidia-ceo--9a4d2ab0e9b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261123-jensen-huang-reinstated-as-nvidia-ceo" /><summary type="html">In a stunning U-turn, Nvidia's board has reinstated Jensen Huang as the company's President and CEO. The announcement came just days after the board rejected a petition calling for the tech titan's return. US President Donald Trump said had personally got in touch with the board to advocate for his return. Nvidia's stock surged 32%, adding nearly $1 trillion to its market cap while the rest of Wall Street also rallied.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>'A war of unmanned machines, AI and total transparency of the battlefield'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdd8080910fbe36d5548d34ad9c09d06d7f29711fd8f499bbaa0d4cadd169879</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T21:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261123-a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield--b335b8ca1842.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261123-a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that today's war in Ukraine "is a war of unmanned machines, AI, total transparency of the battlefield, mass drones attacks and long range weapons, and this means we have to rethink how to protect human beings".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>'A war of unmanned machines, AI and total transparency of the battlefield'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acd1942f0f871b8f05328691daa43ea56bbaffcf990458103fefaf8d29827a21</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T21:54:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield--4945328f5666.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that today's war in Ukraine "is a war of unmanned machines, AI, total transparency of the battlefield, mass drones attacks and long range weapons, and this means we have to rethink how to protect human beings".</summary></entry><entry><title>Libya's east seeks UN probe into claims Ukrainian military present in west</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a17ef77a0f37fed6acc10e48da560c8522e6f6c8b9c96fdf3e2d9e3f8184ced</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T20:08:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/libya-s-east-seeks-un-probe-into-claims-ukrainian-military-present-in-west--6cb055560ea5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/libya-s-east-seeks-un-probe-into-claims-ukrainian-military-present-in-west" /><summary type="html">Authorities in divided Libya's east called on Monday for the United Nations to investigate claims that Ukrainian forces were present in the country's west, as they lodged a complaint over Ukrainian attacks on two Russian ships off Benghazi. The strikes on Sunday, claimed by Kyiv, come as Ukraine steps up strikes against Russia far from the front lines of their war. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump backs Nvidia boss's return but top Democrat vows probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f589dc474b5b766415aa75105fa8c1f6cdc6d70fcd36551a801656fd15d451d</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:53:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-backs-nvidia-boss-s-return-but-top-democrat-vows-probe--0b7b3a362597.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-backs-nvidia-boss-s-return-but-top-democrat-vows-probe" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump praised Nvidia's decision Monday to reinstate Jensen Huang as chief executive, as top Senate Democrat Chuck Schumer vowed to investigate potential wrongdoing amid mounting national security concerns. Trump also posted a doctored version of the famous photograph of him raising his fist after surviving a 2024 assassination attempt, replacing himself with Huang, who brandished a red bra beneath an Nvidia flag. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>How far will Ukraine war spread? Kyiv targets Russian vessels in Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:047f5c950c5199c552dca49dcb73e7b3740226b0163baa5a4bb754060c12436b</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:41:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261123-how-far-will-ukraine-war-spread-kyiv-targets-russian-vessels-in-libya--ff327a037bc6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261123-how-far-will-ukraine-war-spread-kyiv-targets-russian-vessels-in-libya" /><summary type="html">Talk about a spillover effect. In the Libyan port of Benghazi, Ukraine is claiming responsibility for the sinkings first of a Russian warship and then a cargo vessel. That's on top of the sanctioned ship struck in the Baltic Sea that's since strayed into Finland's waters. Are these legitimate targets?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine claims it sank Russian warship off Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b8887930df5eff453233a083602c60b7516ae807de1207f9b7c8965a5901025</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-claims-it-sank-russian-warship-off-libya--1e8645cf71f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-claims-it-sank-russian-warship-off-libya" /><summary type="html">Ukraine on Monday claimed it was behind strikes on two Russian vessels off Libya, including one that sank a modern warship, in the latest spillover from Moscow's invasion. The attacks on Sunday near the Libyan port of Benghazi come at a time when Ukraine has stepped up its daring strikes against Russia far from the frontlines in retaliation for Moscow's deadly invasion. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia reinstates Huang as CEO after Trump intervention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38158758dad9fb095f7fa93812ce1218a6b8aaa764f0562054b9937b8d683753</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:34:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-huang-as-ceo-after-trump-intervention--fe676549fe07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-huang-as-ceo-after-trump-intervention" /><summary type="html">Nvidia on Monday reinstated Jensen Huang as chief executive in a stunning reversal that President Donald Trump said followed his own direct contacts with the company's board. Huang resigned two weeks ago over an affair with a woman whom US intelligence agencies suspect of spying for China, a departure that sent Wall Street tumbling and stoked fears for a US economy reliant on the AI investment boom. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland and Wassim Cornet report.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Maintain control': UN chief calls for creation of global AI safety framework within a year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d202f3a320c420a5c086b1749959d9ba30d78c40720d0eedb4d12bc24dd93c7</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:06:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-un-chief-antonio-guterres-calls-for-global-ai-safety-framework-within-a-year--b8cbcdfbe9c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-un-chief-antonio-guterres-calls-for-global-ai-safety-framework-within-a-year" /><summary type="html">UN chief Antonio Guterres on Monday urged countries to agree on the creation of a global framework for managing the dangers posed by artificial intelligence within one year. Speaking at a summit in Barbados, he warned that taming the technology is vital if humanity is to stay in charge of its own future.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Deeply shocked': Gisèle Pelicot to sue publisher after nude photos used in book campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d5f517faf348c291c3e9e8d5efc832cf81a2c8c86fd488b403c98cbad68a930</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T17:52:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261123-deeply-shocked-gis_le-pelicot-sue-publisher-nude-photos-used-book-campaign--95cd2eb6d7ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261123-deeply-shocked-gis%C3%A8le-pelicot-sue-publisher-nude-photos-used-book-campaign" /><summary type="html">French feminist icon Gisèle Pelicot, who became a worldwide symbol against sexual violence during the 2024 rape trials against her husband and dozens of other men, said Monday she will take legal action after nude images of her were sent out without her permission to publicise a psychoanalyst's book on coercive control.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Finland summons Russian ambassador after suspected airspace violation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:107e9d0b154c843ee9aec619d6310009ca1b4b8af37e9ea0964a9d3aae2c999d</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:50:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-finland-summons-russian-ambassador-after-suspected-airspace-violation--777165c768bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-finland-summons-russian-ambassador-after-suspected-airspace-violation" /><summary type="html">Finland on Monday said it had summoned Russia's ambassador over a suspected violation of Finnish airspace by a Russian helicopter and after a Ukrainian drone strike on a Russian cargo ship located in the Gulf of Finland in recent days. Helsinki also condemned Moscow's escalating strikes on civilian targets in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
